      "description": "Requires an iPhone running iOS 18 or later, paired with Apple Watch running watchOS 11 or later.\n\nTurn wrist motion into music.\n\nPretend Piano lets you play your music on Apple Watch with gestures. Strum for guitar, move your wrist like a bow for violin, or gently tap a tabletop to play piano.\n\nTHREE WAYS TO PLAY\n• Guitar: gently move your wrist up and down to strum chords.\n• Violin: move your wrist side to side to play notes with bow-like gestures.\n• Piano: gently tap a tabletop near your watch wrist to play the next note.\n\nMAKE AND SEND SONGS\nUse iPhone to enter numbered notation, arrange notes and chords, Check and edit the result, then send your song to Apple Watch.\n\nPLAY ON YOUR WRIST\nMotion processing and instrument sounds run locally on Apple Watch. No account is required. Your iPhone does not need to be nearby while you play.\n\nUse gentle movements and taps, and keep a steady rhythm.",
